        "id": "p23-q26-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Solve\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{3}&=1\\\\\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{y}{4}&=1.\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(-6,12)$.",
          "worked": "Clear the denominators:\n$$\\begin{align*}3x+2y&=6\\qquad(1)\\\\4x+3y&=12\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nEliminate $y$ using $3(1)-2(2)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(9x+6y)-(8x+6y)&=18-24\\\\x&=-6.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}3(-6)+2y&=6\\\\2y&=24\\\\y&=12.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y)=(-6,12)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q26-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p23-q26-b-introduction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
